{"Title":"An Act to expand access to computer science coursework","BillNumber":"H445","DocketNumber":"HD3571","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"M_C3","Name":"Manny Cruz","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/M_C3","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T12:01:07.33"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"M_C3","Name":"Manny Cruz","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/M_C3","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T12:01:07.33"},{"Id":"AXV1","Name":"Andres X. Vargas","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/AXV1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T13:29:20.8466667"},{"Id":"S_G2","Name":"Steven Ultrino","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/S_G2","ResponseDate":"2023-02-14T07:34:30.82"},{"Id":"CMM1","Name":"Christopher M. Markey","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/CMM1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-22T09:39:03.3733333"},{"Id":"REH1","Name":"Russell E. Holmes","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/REH1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-23T12:01:19.2433333"},{"Id":"DFD1","Name":"David F. DeCoste","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/DFD1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-23T12:01:19.2433333"}],"JointSponsor":{"Id":"AXV1","Name":"Andres X. Vargas","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/AXV1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T12:01:07.33"},"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H445/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representatives Cruz of Salem and Vargas of Haverhill, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 445) of Manny Cruz, Andres X. Vargas and others for legislation to expand access to computer science coursework in public schools.  Education.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Chapter 71 of the General Laws is amended by inserting after section 99 the following section:- \r\n\tSection 100. Computer Science Education \r\n\t(a) Every public high school in the commonwealth shall offer at least one foundational computer science course and ensure that every student has the capacity to access such course within a four-year course of study.  \r\n\t(b) A foundational computer science course offered pursuant to this section shall include rigorous mathematical or scientific concepts and be consistent with standards adopted by the board of elementary and secondary education.  \r\n\tSECTION 2.  Section 1 shall take effect for the school year beginning after July 1, 2025.  \r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J14","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J14"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}